+**Formulas:**
+For each triangular face with vertices $V_1, V_2, V_3$, the outward normal is $\mathbf{n} = (V_2 - V_1) \times (V_3 - V_1)$ [S2]. The signed distance from $P$ to the plane is $D = \mathbf{n} \cdot (P - V_1)$ [S2]. If $\mathbf{n}$ points outward, an interior point yields $D < 0$ [S2].
